00:00:01,915 --> 00:00:03,999
Chapter 93.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,878
The Castaway.

3
00:00:06,879 --> 00:00:11,115
It was but some few days after encountering the Frenchmen that a most

4
00:00:11,116 --> 00:00:16,079
significant event befell the most insignificant of the Peekquad's crew. An

5
00:00:16,080 --> 00:00:21,198
event most lamentable and which ended in providing the sometimes madly merry and

6
00:00:21,199 --> 00:00:26,159
predestinated craft with a living and ever accompanying prophecy of whatever

7
00:00:26,160 --> 00:00:29,435
shattered sequel might prove her own.

8
00:00:29,436 --> 00:00:34,399
Now in the whale ship it is not everyone that goes in the boats. Some few hands

9
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:39,039
are reserved called shipkeepers, whose province it is to work the vessel while

10
00:00:39,040 --> 00:00:43,755
the boats are pursuing the whale. As a general thing, these shipkeepers are as

11
00:00:43,756 --> 00:00:48,558
hearty fellows as the men comprising the boat's crew. But if there happens to be

12
00:00:48,559 --> 00:00:53,999
an unduly slender, clumsy, or timmerous white in the ship, that white is certain

13
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,878
to be made a shipkeeper. It was so in the Peekquad with the little negro

14
00:00:58,879 --> 00:01:02,558
Pippen by nickname, Pip by abbreviation.

15
00:01:02,559 --> 00:01:05,274
Poor Pip. You have heard of him before.

16
00:01:05,275 --> 00:01:11,359
You must remember his tambourine on that dramatic midnight so gloomy jolly.

17
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:17,115
In outer aspect, Pip and Doughboy made a match like a black pony and a white one,

18
00:01:17,116 --> 00:01:21,198
of equal developments, though of dissimilar color, driven in one

19
00:01:21,199 --> 00:01:26,878
eccentric span. But while Hapless Doughboy was by nature dull and torpid

20
00:01:26,879 --> 00:01:31,274
in his intellects, Pip, though over tender-hearted, was at bottom very

21
00:01:31,275 --> 00:01:36,238
bright, with that pleasant, genial, jolly brightness peculiar to his tribe,

22
00:01:36,239 --> 00:01:41,115
a tribe which ever enjoy all holidays and festivities, with finer, freer

23
00:01:41,116 --> 00:01:46,238
relish than any other race. For blacks, the year's calendar should show not but

24
00:01:46,239 --> 00:01:50,399
365 Fourth of July and New Year's days.

25
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:54,878
Nor smile so while I write that this little black was brilliant, for even

26
00:01:54,879 --> 00:02:00,159
blackness has its brilliancancy. Behold yawn lustrous ebony panled in king's

27
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:05,755
cabinets. But Pip loved life and all life's peaceable securities, so that the

28
00:02:05,756 --> 00:02:10,238
panicstriking business in which he had somehow unaccountably become entrapped

29
00:02:10,239 --> 00:02:13,198
had most sadly blurred his brightness.

30
00:02:13,199 --> 00:02:18,558
Though, as he long will be seen, what was thus temporarily subdued in him, in

31
00:02:18,559 --> 00:02:23,999
the end was destined to be luridly illuminated by strange wild fires that

32
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:28,954
fictitiously showed him off to 10 times the natural luster with which, in his

33
00:02:28,955 --> 00:02:33,435
native Talin County in Connecticut, he had once enlivened many of Fiddler's

34
00:02:33,436 --> 00:02:38,954
frolic on the green, and at melodious even tide, with his gay haha, had turned

35
00:02:38,955 --> 00:02:43,594
the round horizon into one starbelled tambourine.

36
00:02:43,595 --> 00:02:48,634
So though in the clear air of day, suspended against a blue veined neck,

37
00:02:48,635 --> 00:02:53,198
the pure watered diamond drop will healthful glow, yet when the cunning

38
00:02:53,199 --> 00:02:57,679
jeweler would show you the diamond in its most impressive luster, he lays it

39
00:02:57,680 --> 00:03:02,878
against a gloomy ground, and then lights it up, not by the sun, but by some

40
00:03:02,879 --> 00:03:09,594
unnatural gases. Then come out those fiery eulgences, infernally superb. Then

41
00:03:09,595 --> 00:03:14,634
the evil blazing diamond, once the divinest symbol of the crystal skies,

42
00:03:14,635 --> 00:03:19,755
looks like some crown jewel stolen from the king of hell. But led us to the

43
00:03:19,756 --> 00:03:25,594
story. It came to pass that in the Amberress affair, Stubs after Orsman

44
00:03:25,595 --> 00:03:30,795
chanced so to sprain his hand, as for a time to become quite maimed, and

45
00:03:30,796 --> 00:03:33,914
temporarily Pip was put in his place.

46
00:03:33,915 --> 00:03:38,558
The first time Stub lowered with him, Pip evinced much nervousness, but

47
00:03:38,559 --> 00:03:43,198
happily for that time escaped close contact with the whale, and therefore

48
00:03:43,199 --> 00:03:48,159
came off not altogether discreditably, though Stub, observing him, took care

49
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:52,954
afterwards to exhort him to cherish his courageousness to the utmost, for he

50
00:03:52,955 --> 00:03:55,679
might often find it needful.

51
00:03:55,680 --> 00:04:00,878
Now upon the second lowering, the boat paddled upon the whale, and as the fish

52
00:04:00,879 --> 00:04:05,679
received the darted iron, it gave its customary wrap, which happened in this

53
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:10,719
instance to be right under poor Pip's seat. The involuntary consternation of

54
00:04:10,720 --> 00:04:15,838
the moment caused him to leap, paddle in hand, out of the boat, and in such a way

55
00:04:15,839 --> 00:04:20,238
that part of the slack whale line coming against his chest, he breasted it

56
00:04:20,239 --> 00:04:24,878
overboard with him, so as to become entangled in it, when at last plumping

57
00:04:24,879 --> 00:04:29,518
into the water. That instant these stricken whales started on a fierce run.

58
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:34,795
The line swiftly straightened and presto, poor Pip, came all foaming up to

59
00:04:34,796 --> 00:04:39,039
the chocks of the boat, remorselessly dragged there by the line which had

60
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:45,274
taken several turns around his chest and neck. Tashego stood in the boughs. He

61
00:04:45,275 --> 00:04:50,479
was full of the fire of the hunt. He hated Pip for a poultrune. Snatching the

62
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:55,198
boat knife from its sheath, he suspended its sharp edge over the line, and

63
00:04:55,199 --> 00:05:01,115
turning toward Stub, exclaimed interrogatively, "Cut." Meanwhile, Pip's

64
00:05:01,116 --> 00:05:07,518
blue choked face plainly looked, "Do for God's sake." All passed in a flash. In

65
00:05:07,519 --> 00:05:13,679
less than half a minute, this entire thing happened. "Damn him! Cut!" roared

66
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:19,039
Stub. And so, the whale was lost, and Pip was saved.

67
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:23,679
So soon as he recovered himself, the poor little negro was assailed by yells

68
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:28,954
and execrations from the crew. Tranquil permitting these irregular cursings to

69
00:05:28,955 --> 00:05:33,838
evaporate, Stub then, in a plain business-like but still half humorous

70
00:05:33,839 --> 00:05:38,795
manner, cursed Pip officially, and that done unofficially gave him much

71
00:05:38,796 --> 00:05:45,198
wholesome advice. The substance was never jump from a boat, Pip. Except, but

72
00:05:45,199 --> 00:05:50,238
all the rest was indefinite as the soundest advice ever is. Now, in

73
00:05:50,239 --> 00:05:55,594
general, stick to the boat is your true motto in whailing. But cases will

74
00:05:55,595 --> 00:06:00,719
sometimes happen when leap from the boat is still better. Moreover, as if

75
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:05,115
perceiving at last that if he should give undiluted conscientious advice to

76
00:06:05,116 --> 00:06:10,399
Pip, he would be leaving him too wide a margin to jump in for the future, Stub

77
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:14,399
